  "body": "This spacious and light-filled family home will appeal instantly - exceptional location, fabulous floorplan, architecturally designed to nurture and enhance family living.  Enjoy sensational outdoor flow and wide views and be impressed by the ambiance and immaculate presentation. Walk right in and fall in love!\r\n\r\nNestled on a landscaped freehold 630m2 (more or less), in an exclusive green enclave, Francis Clarke Architects have designed the perfect family home, and maximised the outlook to the Gulf, all-day sun, and superb outdoor flow to expansive decks and a private courtyard. 32A Castor Bay Road is private, peaceful, and just minutes from gorgeous beaches, vibrant local amenities, schools, and transport links.\r\n\r\nEnjoying 26 most pleasurable years since new in this wonderfully presented and maintained home, it's time for the next chapter- downsizing - which offers the next lucky owner options for living including:\r\n\r\ni)\tgrow your family in the best school zones\r\nii)\tmove Mum and Dad in;\r\niii)\trun your business from here/work from home.\r\n\r\nBuilt in 2000, the exterior is a solid plaster system (no cavity). The vendors offer a Presale Building and Watertightness Report, a LIM and the Council Property Files for your confidence and encourage you to conduct your own investigations as a condition of purchase.  An eventual reclad to enhance the re-sale value would be a good option.  There is no flood zone or overland flow path to affect this home.\r\n\r\n2024 CV $1,950,000 is based on a recent QV formal inspection and valuation.\r\n \r\nThe double front doors sweep you into the welcoming foyer featuring a double-height void, with overhead skylight and a striking suspended light feature. Mezzanine windows above provide intriguing architectural connections to the upper level, including the private master suite, which offers a true sanctuary. Generously proportioned and thoughtfully separated from the remainder of the home, it features a private balcony, walk-in wardrobe and a stylish contemporary ensuite finished with full tiling and enhanced by natural light.\r\n\r\nThe home's primary living spaces unfold beneath soaring ceilings and strategically positioned skylights. The family room and dining area flow through to the lounge with gorgeous gas fireplace, and both living areas open wide to the sun-soaked decks, all weather entertaining spaces, and a paved courtyard with BBQ and wonderful spa.  Views from the living spaces and the deck extend across the surrounding neighbourhood out to the Gulf, an ever-changing coastal backdrop. A powder room at this level is a thoughtful design feature.\r\n\r\nThe double garage at entry level with internal access provides plenty of storage and a workshop area, and there's additional off-street parking for 2 or 3 including a motor home or boat.\r\n\r\nThree generously proportioned double bedrooms on entry level enjoy excellent separation and privacy, open directly outdoors, and share an elegant family bathroom (both shower and spa bath), and a separate WC.  At this level is a truly spacious laundry and generous under-stair storage - combining practical convenience for everyday living.\r\n\r\nFew Auckland suburbs rival the enduring appeal of Castor Bay. Known for its beautiful local beaches, established prestige homes and relaxed coastal atmosphere, the area continues to attract families seeking an exceptional lifestyle and prestigious school zones.   Well-designed homes allowing families to grow into them and/or offering work from home options are rarely available in this prestigious location, so don't miss viewing this wonderful home.\r\n\r\nCall me now, Tip Spooner 021366710 for further information and a private viewing, or stroll into the Open Homes Saturday/Sunday 12.15-1pm - you'll be so glad you did!",
